requirement art 3 micro undertaking definition is identified by "http://data.europa.eu/leg/lomo/financial-reporting#Requirement_Art3_MicroUndertakingDefinition".

requirement art 3 micro undertaking definition has the type "owl:NamedIndividual".

requirement art 3 micro undertaking definition is a constitutive rule.

requirement art 3 micro undertaking definition has the label "Article 3(1) - Micro-undertakings Definition".

requirement art 3 micro undertaking definition has the digital dimension observation.

requirement art 3 micro undertaking definition defines def micro undertaking.

requirement art 3 micro undertaking definition is established in "http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/2013/34/oj/art_3/par_1".

requirement art 3 micro undertaking definition has the legal text "In applying one or more of the options in Article 36, Member States shall define micro-undertakings as undertakings which on their balance sheet dates do not exceed the limits of at least two of the three following criteria:
(a) balance sheet total: EUR 350 000;
(b) net turnover: EUR 700 000;
(c) average number of employees during the financial year: 10.".

requirement art 3 micro undertaking definition has the comment "Constitutive rule defining micro-undertakings by size thresholds (€350k balance sheet, €700k turnover, 10 employees).".


requirement art 3 small undertaking definition is identified by "http://data.europa.eu/leg/lomo/financial-reporting#Requirement_Art3_SmallUndertakingDefinition".

requirement art 3 small undertaking definition has the type "owl:NamedIndividual".

requirement art 3 small undertaking definition is a constitutive rule.

requirement art 3 small undertaking definition has the label "Article 3(2) - Small Undertakings Definition".

requirement art 3 small undertaking definition has the digital dimension observation.

requirement art 3 small undertaking definition defines def small undertaking.

requirement art 3 small undertaking definition is established in "http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/2013/34/oj/art_3/par_2".

requirement art 3 small undertaking definition has the legal text "Small undertakings shall be undertakings which on their balance sheet dates do not exceed the limits of at least two of the three following criteria:
(a) balance sheet total: EUR 4 000 000;
(b) net turnover: EUR 8 000 000;
(c) average number of employees during the financial year: 50.
Member States may define thresholds exceeding the thresholds in points (a) and (b) of the first subparagraph. However, the thresholds shall not exceed EUR 6 000 000 for the balance sheet total and EUR 12 000 000 for the net turnover.".

requirement art 3 small undertaking definition has the comment "Constitutive rule defining small undertakings by size thresholds (€4M/€6M balance sheet, €8M/€12M turnover, 50 employees).".


